    "result_text": "All 17 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment rule. On owner creation, the code is formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` \u2014 the upper-cased first three letters of the last name, a hyphen, and a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current owner count.\n\nChanges:\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field (`customer_code` column) with getter/setter.\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added `nextCustomerCode(lastName)` and assign it in `addOwner` right before `saveOwner` (after validation/conflict checks, so rejected creates don't consume a number). Sequence = `findAllOwners().size() + 1`, formatted with `%s-%04d`.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `customerCode` as a read-only property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct maps it by name into the GET response.\n- **`db/hsqldb|h2|mysql|postgres/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column (the test profile is `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the DDL had to carry the column; I updated the other dialects for consistency).\n\nThe new `Cp09Tests` (SMI-/JON- prefixes and consecutive global sequence) passes, and all pre-existing acceptance tests remain green.",
